.pytest_cache
__pycache__/
.coverage
.venv/
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
# .vscode/ is deliberately TRACKED. It used to be ignored (as *.vscode*),
# so the editor config was local-only: when VS Code lost the cached
# interpreter the settings could not restore it, and Pylance fell back to a
# system python with no homeassistant installed, which surfaced as dozens of
# bogus "could not be resolved" import errors.
# Personal overrides that should stay local:
.vscode/*.local.json
.github/**/*instruction*
*samples*
# pyrightconfig.json is tracked on purpose: without an explicit pythonVersion,
# Pylance falls back to <=3.13 and cannot parse the project's PEP 758
# `except A, B:` syntax, producing bogus "has no attribute" errors.
# Local editor overrides stay ignored.
pyrightconfig.local.json
*.log
*diag-sample.json*
*translate.py*
*claude*
*subtask*
